cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use qmutate in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "qmutate: mutation testing for Qiskit quantum circuits"
abstract: >-
  qmutate is a pre-alpha Python library for mutation testing of quantum circuits built with
  Qiskit. It removes one top-level instruction at a time from a circuit, runs a user-supplied
  test oracle against every mutant, and reports the outcomes and a mutation score. It also
  provides numerical equivalence checks for an equivalence-adjusted score and a finite-shot
  sampling oracle whose verdicts carry statistical guarantees under stated assumptions.
